Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:44:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] Finder: log where the window is stuck when it hangs

A watchdog thread expects a heartbeat from the GUI thread ten times a
second. Stalls of about 300 ms or more get a line in
~/.local/state/finder/hangs.log, with the folder being shown. Hangs past
half a second also get the GUI thread's stack from eu-stack, and more
stacks while the hang goes on. Finder and the Open/Save dialog both log
there. FINDER_HANGWATCH=0 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
